WEBVTT

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.730
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.360
<i>Jean met Nadia and King, Nadia's
pet lion cub, at the Paris Expo.</i>

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.610
<i>They were attacked by an evil trio
after Nadia's Blue Water gem.</i>

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.370
<i>They barely escaped in an airplane
invented by Jean.</i>

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:45.250
<i>After many escapades, they were
forced to land on an island which was</i>

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:50.420
<i>the secret base for a sinister
organization called Neo Atlantis.</i>

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.460
<i>On this island, Jean and Nadia
met a little girl named Marie.</i>

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.300
<i>Nadia, Marie and King became
captives of Neo Atlantis.</i>

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.510
<i>Nadia met the masked leader,
Gargoyle, who calls her Princess.</i>

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.390
<i>She was forced to witness a test of
the fearsome Tower of Babel weapon.</i>

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.610
<i>This weapon has the power to easily
destroy an entire island.</i>

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.280
<i>After a fearsome battle, the secret
base was destroyed</i>

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.530
<i>through the actions of Jean and Nadia,</i>

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:22.490
<i>assisted by Grandis's gang and the
Nautilus commanded by Captain Nemo.</i>

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.760
I wonder if the island people
are all right?

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.880
I think so. They were all gathering
on the beach.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.760
Now that Gargoyle's forces have left,
they should be all right.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.810
I guess you're right. I'm glad.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.480
Hey, Jean!

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.990
What are you doing? Come
over here, and help!

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.410
What's up?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.950
There's damage all over,
and we're leaking.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.250
If we don't do something,
my Gratan will sink!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.960
Look what happened to us because
we tried to help you.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.790
I've even caught a cold!

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.130
That's right! We'll ask the
Nautilus to help us.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.510
The Nautilus?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.470
I mean the submarine that
came to rescue us.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:41.860
Captain Nemo, we have received an
S.O.S. from a strange looking tank.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.780
Read it.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.410
Yes, Sir. "Save us! Save us!
Grandis" That's all.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.290
What shall we do?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.040
Rescue them.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.960
Are you sure?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:57.750
Yes, they fought Neo Atlantis with us.
We can't abandon them.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.960
I understand, Sir.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.600
They say they'll help us.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.100
Lucky!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.730
I get another chance to see
that submarine.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:12.810
We have to board that again?

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.070
It sure is big!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.690
Yeah, it sure is.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.490
It's hard to believe a submarine this
huge has already been built.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.200
I can board her again!

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.080
What's wrong? You don't
look very happy.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.790
I don't like that ship.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.420
We'll collect you in our aft hatch.
Move toward that position.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.270
What's that?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.570
Close the hatches!

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.460
The survivors have been picked up.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.170
Good.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.380
Captain, the damage report
has been completed.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.850
Damage on the outside hull is minor.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.220
However, the atomic hydrogen line

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.720
and the magnetic field adjusting
system have sustained major damage.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.180
How long will it take for repairs?

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.640
Forty-eight hours.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.860
Can't you shorten that?

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:42.610
If a professional says it will
take forty-eight hours,

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.650
forty-eight hours is how
long it will take.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:45.990
Carry out a thorough repair job.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:49.820
Yes, Sir. All power circuits on board
have been switched to battery power.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.910
Which means our movements
will be severely restricted.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.620
It can't be helped.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.460
I know you are doing your best.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.250
We can only pray that an emergency
situation will not come up.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.840
My sentiments exactly, Sir.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.840
Carry on.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.340
Yes, Sir.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:10.800
Sir, I regret that we let
Gargoyle escape us.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.970
I'm not giving up.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.100
I'll never give up.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.060
Of course not, Sir. The whole
crew feels the same way.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:25.110
Now then, what shall we do with the
group on board that curious tank?

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.530
If anyone is sick or injured, make
sure they get the best of care.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.820
I'll leave this matter in your
hands. However...

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.830
We can't have any outsiders walking
around inside the ship.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.330
When repairs on the tank
are completed,

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.790
give them plenty of food and water,
and get rid of them.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.040
That's what you meant
to say, isn't it?

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.510
What a bunch of heartless people!

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:54.810
After tying up Katherine,
they go and leave us.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.720
It's not right.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:01.310
Well, I'm thankful they saved us, but
they certainly are unfriendly.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:01.940
Right?

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.360
Look at those two. Why do
they look so happy?

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.070
See? There are no rivets used.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.370
I can't believe it. How did they
connect the edges, I wonder?

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.580
Isn't it amazing? This ship is
full of futuristic science.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.920
It sure is, and we're actually on it!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.090
How lucky we are!

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.880
This is the door?

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.590
Yeah, it opened by itself before.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.480
Miss Electra!

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.940
My, so it's you again.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.360
Welcome to our ship.
Nice to have you on board.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.320
Excuse me...

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:57.950
We are grateful to you
for saving us, Mademoiselle.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.920
Allow me to make introductions.
This is my assistant, Hanson.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.630
Assistant?!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.050
The lady over there is Senorita
Grandis Granba,

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.170
our leader.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:17.180
And I am Sanson, at your service.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:22.390
Sanson, you don't have to identify
yourself to a girl wearing a mask!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.770
You are right. I must apologize.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.980
I am Electra. I am second in
command on this ship.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:39.620
It's nice to see you and Nadia again,
even if it is unexpected.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.370
I'm glad too.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.210
This child?

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:47.250
Her name is Marie. We found
her on the island.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.540
And her parents?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.510
They fell victim to Neo Atlantis.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:57.390
All right, I understand. You are now
under the protection of this ship.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.310
You are not allowed to roam
freely inside the ship.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.350
We shall arrange your room,
and attend to your needs.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:06.850
Have you caught a cold?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.320
Of course! Being cooped up
in a place like this!

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:14.400
Oh, that's not good. I'll call a doctor
for you right away.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.610
Everyone, please come this way.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.950
Gargoyle told you he knew something
about your past?

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:28.040
Yes, and he called the crystal tower,
the Tower of Babel.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.960
The Tower of Babel?
Like the one in the Old Testament?

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:36.680
I don't know about that, but he kept
referring to the orihalcon.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:42.350
Orihalcon? Could it be that big glass
block lying under the tower?

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.430
It looked like the Blue Water.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.640
Really?

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.270
There must be a connection between
the Blue Water, Neo Atlantis,

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.570
and the Nautilus too.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.080
Hey, Hanson, how does it look?

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.750
The lock on this door is either
electrical or magnetic.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.210
It's an amazing invention.
It's impossible to open with a hairpin.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:16.550
This time I'll leave everything to you.
That wall is too tough.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.680
Just look at my hands.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.600
It's no use! I give up!

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:25.060
I see.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.600
I wonder if our leader is okay?

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.070
The doctor on board said it was
just an ordinary cold.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.940
Well then! Let's go and see her.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.360
How are we going to get out?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.200
Simple. We'll just ask.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:39.820
Ask?

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:44.160
Don't be so dense. They must be
listening in on our conversation.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.000
That's true!

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:50.670
That's it!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:59.090
Excuse me! We'd like to go see
our leader now please!

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.220
All right, you may see her.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.140
Lucky!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.180
Ouch!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.140
Miss?

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:14.610
Doctor! Is she all right? If something
should happen to her...

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:19.450
Don't worry. She's sleeping due to the
medicine. She'll be okay tomorrow.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.360
She'll recover in only one day?

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.330
That's amazing! It's a magical medicine.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.160
No, it's the power of science.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.330
This is an incredible ship!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.260
First Officer, what's the repair status?

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.970
On schedule. Repairs on the hull
will be completed by morning.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.760
Were you able to intercept any
messages from Neo Atlantis?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.640
No, Sir.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:52.600
Losing one or two advance bases
doesn't faze them a bit.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.650
Captain, why don't you return to your
cabin, and get a little rest?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.980
I'd rather stay here.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:01.650
With all my men working
day and night,

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.240
how can you expect me to
go to sleep, is that it?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.830
First Officer, you talk a little too much.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:12.210
I must tell you one other thing.
We picked up those kids again.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:16.670
Kids? You mean the ones
who built the airplane?

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.800
I wouldn't have left them if I'd known
that island was Gargoyle's.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.090
I feel bad about that.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.550
You're not going to see them
this time either?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.390
There's no need to.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.140
I see...

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:44.360
I wonder where I'll be going to next?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.670
Repair work on the hull
has been completed.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:01.380
Thanks, why don't you get some rest?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:06.890
No, I'm all right. But Miss
Grandis is awake now.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.800
I see.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:11.770
What is this?!

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.980
They told me it was milk.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.480
It has a strange tangy taste.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.030
It's supposed to be full of nourishment.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.190
What kind of milk is it?

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.820
It's whale's milk.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:31.700
Whale's milk? Do they expect a high
class lady like me to drink this?!

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.750
Excuse me, may we come in?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.960
Who are you?

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.380
Let me introduce myself.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:41.050
I'm the captain of this ship.
My name is Nemo.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.510
Oh, my!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.630
I just want to say a few words.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:46.470
Yes!

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.890
How do you feel today?

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:52.850
Oh, just fine, thanks to your kindness!

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:58.350
I'm very happy to hear that. We
shall fix up your tank also.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.320
When it's ready, you are free to
leave whenever you like.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.280
Oh no, we can fix it up by ourselves.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:07.740
I understand. Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.120
May I have your name again, please?

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.490
It's Nemo. Good day.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.580
Nemo... Captain Nemo.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.000
What about that?

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:27.130
She was acting funny.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:27.880
What, again?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.840
I'm pretty sure. I've seen that
look many times before.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.350
You mean she...

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.770
Has the look of love again?!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.690
She can be a headache at times.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.110
It happens whenever she meets
a middle-aged gentleman.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:48.900
What's so appealing about a
middle-aged guy like that?

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.660
Now, look here!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:58.290
Fix up the Gratan in a hurry, will you?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:14:59.750
Why?

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.710
Because we have to leave
as quickly as possible.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.170
Leave?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:08.760
Of course! We have to get
her away from Nemo.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:09.590
But...

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.550
But? But what?!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.510
There's so much we can learn about
science and technology.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:21.440
The way I figure it, this ship is in a
fight with this guy, Gargoyle.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.480
We can get killed at any time.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.650
But Miss Electra is such a nice lady.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.110
What?!

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.570
You get taken away by any
good looking dame!

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.530
No, I don't.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.540
Which one appeals to you more,
Grandis or Electra?

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.210
Could it be...

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.540
Well...

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.880
What? What was that?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.880
It's...

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.420
What was that?

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.590
Our leader.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:55.180
Good! Then you'll help me with
my plans to escape?

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.350
That's settled then.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.640
Okay! Let's get started, Hanson!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.770
Say, Nadia...

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.230
Let's go and visit Grandis.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.190
Why should we?

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:12.150
Well, Sanson and Hanson both
seem to be good people.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:16.240
Those three helped to rescue
you and Marie and King.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.740
Why do you think they helped us?

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:22.040
The situation just called for it.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.290
Geez! They only helped us
to steal my Blue Water!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.750
That's the only reason!

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:28.920
I don't know.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.380
Geez!

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:34.840
But all the time I was with them, the
Blue Water didn't shine once.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.720
Then it was broken.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.470
That's hard to believe.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:43.350
Then, it must be in my hands
for it to shine!

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.060
Maybe you're right.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.570
What's wrong, King?

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.110
Caught a cold?

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.570
Are you well, King?

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.530
Open your mouth. That's a good boy.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.700
This is terrible! His throat is
swollen up! What'll I do?

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.080
You must go to a doctor. That's what
Mama used to say.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.580
You're right, Marie. Thanks.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.750
The quicker the better.
Let's go right away.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.550
We can see Grandis at the same time.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.510
We're only concerned with King.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:20.180
Get this straight! We're going to
persuade her to leave this ship.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:21.520
But...

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:26.770
It's always the same. Either she gets
tired of him, or he dumps her.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.690
If her love is not going to
be fulfilled anyway,

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.480
it's better to separate them
as early as possible.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:31.610
But...

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:38.200
If a lion catches cold, can he give
it to humans too, I wonder?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.410
What're you doing here?

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.580
It seems King caught a little cold.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.170
After that, we thought we'd
look in on Grandis.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:53.920
We appreciate your visit, but
could you wait a bit?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.130
We have some important
matters to discuss first.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.300
Our business is important too!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.100
Look! The Blue Water isn't shining.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.060
That's because Grandis isn't here!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.520
Hey, hey, what are you
two quarreling about?

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.100
It has nothing to do with you!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.480
You mustn't quarrel!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:22.620
Jean, Nadia, we are all friends.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:27.960
Nadia, I'm sorry we chased
after you like we did.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.090
You don't have to worry
about that anymore.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.210
Sanson, Hanson...

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.460
Yes.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:38.930
I've decided to remain on this
ship for a while longer.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.720
Now, if all of you will
please excuse me.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.480
This is serious!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.770
She means it this time.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.440
Sanson, Hanson, are you coming?

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.900
Yes, Ma'am!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.160
What just happened?

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.580
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.760
What a relief. You'll feel better now, King.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.470
Poor King.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:21.680
Come to me, King.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.390
Let's go!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.230
Oh, why are all of you here?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.520
We were just...

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:36.110
Let me introduce you.
This is the boy, Jean.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:41.610
Glad to meet you, Sir! Thank you for
rescuing us, Commander Nemo!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.450
I... I...

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.370
Jean, is it?

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:46.830
Yes, Sir!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.200
Do not call me commander!

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.710
This is not a warship.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:54.580
I see. I'm sorry, Sir.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.590
If you'll excuse me...

00:19:56.590 --> 00:20:01.300
And this is Marie and King, the
baby lion, and this is Nadia.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.440
Nadia! It can't be!

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.900
You are not allowed to walk around
the ship without permission.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.510
He's just as I pictured him.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.970
Captain Nemo is a strong man.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:50.640
A true sailor! Don't you
think so too, Nadia?

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:56.190
Nadia?

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:58.900
I'm sorry.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.230
Is something wrong?

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.400
No, it's nothing.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.570
Nadia...

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:05.530
Have you caught a cold too?

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:10.120
No. No, I haven't, Marie.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.620
It's nothing. It's really nothing.

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:09.590
It sure is noisy. What is that?

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.140
Sounds like a pipe organ.

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:22.480
Mother...

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:53.510
No, you mustn't!

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:00.020
Nadia, why did you come here?

00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:04.860
When I heard this music,

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:08.320
I felt as if my mother was calling me.

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:10.700
Get a hold of yourself, Nadia!

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:12.160
But...

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:15.740
That's Captain Nemo playing.

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:17.120
Now, let's go back.

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:18.870
Captain Nemo?

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:22.210
Yes, this is his cabin.

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:24.590
No one is allowed to enter.
